$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
yubikey-turnkey: error: site.toml: Expected '=' after a key in a key/value pair (at line 1, column 5)
[exit 2]

$ yubikey-turnkey missing.toml
yubikey-turnkey: error: cannot read missing.toml: No such file or directory
[exit 2]

$ yubikey-turnkey --check --renew-certs site.toml
yubikey-turnkey: error: --check changes nothing: not with --renew-certs
[exit 2]

$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: [site]: missing
site.toml: [[server]]: there must be exactly three servers
site.toml: [anycast]: missing
site.toml: [admin]: missing
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# two servers
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: [[server]]: there must be exactly three servers
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# the same name, address and router twice; a router with two AS numbers
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: [[server]]: name 'a' is used twice
site.toml: [[server]]: ipv4 '192.0.2.1' is used twice
site.toml: server[2].router: router '192.0.2.254' has two AS numbers
site.toml: server[2].router: router '2001:db8::fe' has two AS numbers
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# addresses that aren't, or can't be
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: server[1].ipv4: '192.0.2.300' is not an IPv4 address
site.toml: server[2].ipv6: '192.0.2.9' is not an IPv6 address
site.toml: server[3].ipv4: '127.0.0.1' can't be used here
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# the anycast addresses a server's, the servers' AS a router's
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: anycast.asn: 64500 is a router's AS too: the servers need an AS of their own
site.toml: [anycast]: '192.0.2.1' is a server's own address
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# the first server the last resort; two last resorts
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: server[1].last_resort: the first server is the usual primary: it can't be the last resort
site.toml: [[server]]: only one server can be the last resort
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# no router for a; three for c
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: server[1].router: each server needs one or two [[server.router]]
site.toml: server[3].router: each server needs one or two [[server.router]]
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# names and settings
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: site.colour: unknown setting
site.toml: server[2].fqdn: 'b' is not a fully qualified DNS name
site.toml: server[3].name: 'C_1' is not a host name (lower-case letters, digits and '-', up to 31)
site.toml: cluster.wal_keep: '8 GB' is not a size such as 8GB
site.toml: partition.enabled: must be true or false
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# admins
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: admin.logins: 'postgres' can't be an admin's login (lower-case letters, digits and '_'; not postgres, radiator, replicator, rewinder or yubikey_admin)
site.toml: admin.logins: 'ops-admin' can't be an admin's login (lower-case letters, digits and '_'; not postgres, radiator, replicator, rewinder or yubikey_admin)
site.toml: admin.logins: 'a' is listed twice
site.toml: admin.subnets: '10.9.0.1/24' is not a subnet (with the host bits 0) or an address
site.toml: admin.subnets: '0.0.0.0/0' is everything
site.toml: admin.subnets: 'x' is not a subnet (with the host bits 0) or an address
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# devices
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: device[1].group: 'localhost' is reserved
site.toml: device[2].address: '10.1.0.1' is listed twice (device 1)
site.toml: device[3].address: '10.2.0.1/24' is not an address or a subnet (with the host bits 0)
site.toml: device[3].group: 'unlisted' is the catch-all's device group
site.toml: device[4].address: '127.0.0.1' can't be a device (the catch-all takes every device that isn't listed)
site.toml: device[5].address: '::/0' can't be a device (the catch-all takes every device that isn't listed)
site.toml: device[6].group: 'bad group' is not a device group name (letters, digits and . _ -)
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# no devices and no catch-all
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: [[device]]: list the devices, or enable the catch-all client
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# backups: no certificate, keep out of range, an unknown setting
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: backup.retain: unknown setting
site.toml: backup.certificate: missing
site.toml: backup.keep: must be a whole number from 1 to 366
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# backups: missing.crt
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: backup.certificate: cannot read <WORK>/missing.crt: No such file or directory (make it as the guide's "Turn-key backups" says, and keep its private key elsewhere)
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# backups: text.crt
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: backup.certificate: <WORK>/text.crt is not one certificate (PEM)
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# backups: with-key.crt
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: backup.certificate: <WORK>/with-key.crt holds a private key: name a file with the certificate only, and keep the key off the servers
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# backups: ec.crt
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: backup.certificate: <WORK>/ec.crt must have an RSA key of 3072 bits or more
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# backups: small.crt
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: backup.certificate: <WORK>/small.crt must have an RSA key of 3072 bits or more
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# backups: two.crt
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: backup.certificate: <WORK>/two.crt is not one certificate (PEM)
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

# groups
$ yubikey-turnkey site.toml
site.toml: group[1].name: 'anycast-check' is the anycast check's own group
site.toml: group[2].access[1].level: must be a whole number from 0 to 15
site.toml: group[2].access[2].devices: 'nowhere' is not a device group (one of: *, core, localhost, unlisted)
site.toml: group[2].access[3].devices: 'core' is listed twice
site.toml: group[2].access[3].rules: 'allow everything' is not a rule (permit, permitreplace or deny, then patterns; no double quotes or octal escapes)
site.toml: group[2].access[3].rules: 'permit cmd="x"' is not a rule (permit, permitreplace or deny, then patterns; no double quotes or octal escapes)
site.toml: group[3].name: 'ops' is listed twice
yubikey-turnkey: error: nothing written: fix the input first
[exit 2]

